Developer Guide
===============

Getting Started
---------------

Install Java 8.

Run `./sbt run` to start the web app on http://localhost:9000/.

Alternatively, run with Docker:

  docker/build.sh
  docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.local.yml up

This starts both the Play app (port 9000) and Elasticsearch (port 9200) in containers.


Updating Assets
---------------

When updating the bootstrap.js file, concatenate the "Modals", "Dropdowns", "Toggleable tabs" and the "Typeahead" plugins,
and append the bootstrap-fileupload, bootstrap-datepicker and bootstrap-timepicker plugins.

When updating angular-custom.js, append angular-route and angular-sanitize. Remove any "//# sourceMappingURL" lines.

When updating highcharts.js, append highcharts-more.js and modules/exporting.js.

When updating moment.js, append moment-timezone-all-years.js.

When updating Font Awesome, use the unminified css version as the less file, and copy the font files to public/fonts/.

When updating highlight.js, create a custom package with support for bash and json, and copy styles/railscasts.css to
app/assets/css/highlight-railscasts-x.y.less.


Running Tests
-------------

To run all unit tests:

  ./sbt "test-only *Test"

To run a specific test:

  ./sbt "test-only com.zenobase.testing.BrowserTesting"

To skip webdriver tests, set -Dwebdriver.skip=true

To test specific tasks manually:

  1. Find the appropriate *Testing class, e.g. FitbitTesting.

  2. Set up a launch configuration with appropriate oauth.apiKey and oauth.apiSecret system properties.

  3. Run the test. Open the provided URL, complete the authorization, and paste the final URL back into the console.
     Note that IntelliJ has to be started with -Deditable.java.test.console=true in order for this step to work.

  4. Verify the result in the console. Copy the provided oauth.token and oauth.secret system properties into the launch
     configuration to bypass the authorization step in future test runs.


Deploy Procedure
----------------

  1. Push to master. CI runs tests, builds Docker images, and pushes to ECR.

  2. Sign in to AWS with `aws login --profile signin`

  3. If there are infrastructure or configuration changes, update Pulumi config
     (infra/Pulumi.prod.yaml) and/or the secrets (zenobase/prod-conf) first.

     To edit the secrets:

       aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id zenobase/prod-conf \
         --query SecretString --output text > prod.conf

       aws secretsmanager put-secret-value --secret-id zenobase/prod-conf \
         --secret-string file://./prod.conf

  4. Deploy to the inactive target group:

       cd infra
       pulumi config set zenobase:deployTarget green  # or blue
       pulumi up --stack prod

  5. Verify health (monitor in CloudWatch Logs, check ALB target health in AWS console).

  6. Switch traffic:

       pulumi config set zenobase:activeTargetGroup green  # match deployTarget
       pulumi up --stack prod

     This also stops the old instance (preserving its EBS data for quick restarts).

  7. To revert after the switch is complete, set both deployTarget and
     activeTargetGroup back to the old color and run `pulumi up`. The old
     instance will be restarted (takes a few minutes).

To rollback to a specific image version:

  pulumi config set zenobase:playImageTag <sha>
  pulumi up --stack prod


Migration Procedure
-------------------

Use this procedure to rebuild the database (e.g. after data model changes):

  1. Set migration config:

       cd infra
       pulumi config set zenobase:esCluster "<new-cluster-name>"
       pulumi config set zenobase:esReplayCluster "<old-cluster-name>"

  2. Deploy to the inactive target group:

       pulumi config set zenobase:deployTarget green  # or blue
       pulumi up --stack prod

     The new instance starts with an empty ES cluster and replays all commands
     from the old cluster.

  3. Monitor replay progress in CloudWatch Logs.

  4. When replay completes, switch traffic:

       pulumi config set zenobase:activeTargetGroup green  # match deployTarget
       pulumi up --stack prod

  5. Clear migration config for the next deploy:

       pulumi config set zenobase:esReplayCluster ""


Restore Procedure
-----------------

  1. Create a new instance in a new cluster:

       pulumi config set zenobase:deployTarget green  # or blue
       pulumi config set zenobase:esCluster prod-NNN  # new cluster name
       pulumi up --stack prod

  2. Stop the play service:

    cd /opt/zenobase
    sudo docker-compose stop play

  3. Delete all indices:

    curl -XDELETE 'localhost:9200/_all'

  4. Register a snapshot repository, e.g.

    curl -XPUT 'localhost:9200/_snapshot/$OLD_CLUSTER_NAME' -d '{
      "type": "s3",
      "settings": {
          "bucket": "zeno-snapshots",
          "base_path": "$OLD_CLUSTER_NAME"
      }
    }'

  5. List snapshots:

    curl 'localhost:9200/_snapshot/$OLD_CLUSTER_NAME/_all?pretty=true'

  6. Restore a snapshot:

    curl -XPOST 'localhost:9200/_snapshot/$OLD_CLUSTER_NAME/$SNAPSHOT_ID/_restore'

  7. Monitor progress:

    watch curl -s 'localhost:9200/_cat/recovery'

  8. Start the play service:

    sudo docker-compose start play

  9. Switch traffic to the new instance:

    pulumi config set zenobase:activeTargetGroup green  # match deployTarget
    pulumi up --stack prod


SSH Access
----------

SSH is disabled by default (no adminCidr configured in the security group).

To enable temporarily:

  cd infra
  pulumi config set zenobase:adminCidr "$(curl -s ifconfig.me)/32" --stack prod
  pulumi up --stack prod
  ssh -i <key>.pem ec2-user@<ip>

To disable:

  pulumi config rm zenobase:adminCidr --stack prod
  pulumi up --stack prod
